# The FPAC exception (verus/isla/seams.md) in one Armv9.4-A
# configuration: `autda x0, x1` run through, without `--stop-at`. Every
# path falls through (writing x0 only) or takes the exception: then it
# writes no user register (x0 included), no memory and no system register
# but the entry's own, the syndrome is EC 0x1C (FPAC) with IL set and ISS
# 0b10 (a data key, key A), the return address is the `autda` itself,
# PSTATE ends at the kernel's EL (EL1, or EL2 under VHE) on SP_ELx, and
# the PC is that EL's vector for a synchronous exception from a lower EL
# using AArch64, VBAR + 0x400 (bits 55:0; the model clears the top byte of
# a lower-half vector address under TBI, and the kernel's vectors are
# upper-half addresses). run.sh prepends the insn line (kind `fault`) and
# substitutes @EL@ and @LEVEL@.
pc-step
abstract ComputePAC
writes R0
no-mem-write
mem-reads 0
flags-preserved
assert-exc (= final.ESR_@EL@.bits #x0000000072000002)
assert-exc (= final.ELR_@EL@ init._PC)
assert-exc (= ((_ extract 55 0) final._PC) (concat ((_ extract 55 11) init.VBAR_@EL@) #b10000000000))
assert-exc (= final.PSTATE.EL @LEVEL@)
assert-exc (= final.PSTATE.SP #b1)
